PromptSlot variant declaration order is silently load-bearing for concatenation. `#[derive(PartialOrd, Ord)]` ties the build-time sort key directly to enum variant order, so inserting a new variant anywhere except the tail silently rewrites every existing caller's prompt output with zero compile error. Even though the doc comment warns about this, future contributors (or a careless reorder during a refactor) will likely miss it. Consider replacing the derived ordering with an explicit `priority() -> u8` method (or explicit numeric fields) so the order is data-driven, not enum-position-driven — then `sort_by_key(|s| s.priority())` makes the contract self-documenting and reorder-safe.

```rust
impl PromptSlot {
    fn priority(self) -> u8 {
        match self {
            PromptSlot::Base => 0,
            PromptSlot::GenDir => 1,
            PromptSlot::SkillCatalog => 2,
            PromptSlot::SkillBody => 3,
            PromptSlot::Recovery => 4,
            PromptSlot::Plan => 5,
        }
    }
}
```

