`skips_empty_slots` does not actually verify the skip-empty behavior. The empty Plan segment is `""`, and `String::push_str("")` is a no-op — so `assert_eq!(out, "BASERECOVERY")` would pass even if the `if !content.is_empty()` guard were removed. The second assertion `!out.contains("BASERECOVERY\n")` is also trivially true because the builder never inserts separators. The test gives false confidence in a documented invariant. Make the empty content distinguishable from "no content" — e.g., use whitespace that `is_empty()` correctly rejects as empty per the contract, or assert against a non-empty placeholder that would corrupt output if the guard were removed.

```rust
