comments.content:
The Escape handler's effect depends on `onCancel`. In React 18 + StrictMode and any time the parent doesn't `useCallback` the prop, this listener is removed and re-added on every parent render — wasted work, and there is a brief window between remove/add where Escape could be missed. Two fixes worth considering: use a ref to hold the latest `onCancel` and keep an empty-deps effect, or have the parent memoize the handler.

```tsx
const cancelRef2 = useRef(onCancel);
cancelRef2.current = onCancel;
useEffect(() => {
  const onKey = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
    if (e.key === "Escape" && !busy) cancelRef2.current();
  };
  window.addEventListener("keydown", onKey);
  return () => window.removeEventListener("keydown", onKey);
}, [busy]);
```

