comments.content:
**Action handlers have no local refresh / optimistic fallback** (UI staleness risk)

Every action handler in this file (`MemoryCard.act`, `EvolutionCard.enable`/`dismiss`, `ArtifactCard.bind`/`skip`, `WorkflowQuestionCard.respond`, and `NotificationsPage.clearDone`) relies entirely on the backend emitting `NOTIFICATIONS_CHANGED_EVENT` to trigger `reload()`. If the backend fails to emit on any code path (e.g., a new Rust command without the broadcast hook, or an exception in the emit path), the UI stays stale: the card remains in `pending`, the buttons stay enabled, and `busy` flips back to `false` after the await — so the user has no signal that their action took effect and may re-click indefinitely.

At minimum, fire-and-forget `reload()` (or an optimistic local state mutation) after each successful action so the UI converges regardless of event emission. Same applies to `clearDone`, which doesn't even update local state on success.

```ts
const act = async (approve: boolean) => {
  if (ids.length === 0) return;
  setBusy(true);
  try {
    if (approve) await approveMemoryProposals(ids);
    else await rejectMemoryProposals(ids);
    void reload(); // belt-and-suspenders in case NOTIFICATIONS_CHANGED_EVENT is missed
  } catch (e) {
    handleCommandError(e, approve ? "收下记忆提案" : "忽略记忆提案");
  } finally {
    setBusy(false);
  }
};
```

